# env(1)

## NAME

env - run a command in a modified environment

## SYNOPSIS

    env [-i] [-u name]... [name=value]... [command [arg...]]

## DESCRIPTION

Sets the given variables and runs the command. Without a command, prints the resulting environment. The command is looked up in the new `PATH` (or `/bin:/sbin`). A file that is not a WASM program is run as a `/bin/sh` script.

## OPTIONS

- `-i, -`: start with an empty environment (`PWD` is still set by the kernel)
- `-u name`: remove the variable

## EXIT STATUS

- `127`: the command was not found
- `126`: the command could not be started
- `other`: the exit status of the command

## SEE ALSO

printenv(1), sh(1)
